1
00:00:04,468 --> 00:00:04,468
[Intro]

2
00:00:04,468 --> 00:00:09,574
Turn it down!

3
00:00:09,574 --> 00:00:19,574
Nah.

4
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:20,186
[Verse 1]

5
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:22,819
Mom bangs the ceiling like, "Who taught you that?"

6
00:00:22,819 --> 00:00:25,372
Dad shakes his head like the tire went flat.

7
00:00:25,372 --> 00:00:27,846
Borrowed amp humming, a snare with a split,

8
00:00:27,846 --> 00:00:30,399
three chords and a grudge, and we're making it hit.

9
00:00:30,399 --> 00:00:32,952
They paid for the roof and they paid for the floor,

10
00:00:32,952 --> 00:00:35,426
they paid for the lock on the garage door,

11
00:00:35,426 --> 00:00:38,138
but the key's in my pocket, the code's in my head.

12
00:00:38,138 --> 00:00:40,851
They wrote all the rules. We wrote what we said.

13
00:00:40,851 --> 00:00:43,404
Jenny's got bars in the back of her math book.

14
00:00:43,404 --> 00:00:45,957
Sam thumps the bass like he's picking a padlock.

15
00:00:45,957 --> 00:00:48,750
Named the band at 2 a.m. on a dare.

16
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:51,144
Nobody knows what it means. We don't care.

17
00:00:51,144 --> 00:00:53,697
Neighbors call it racket. We call it a rocket,

18
00:00:53,697 --> 00:00:55,771
lit in the driveway, and nobody can stop it.

19
00:00:55,771 --> 00:00:58,803
Report card's on the fridge, but that's not the portrait.

20
00:00:58,803 --> 00:01:02,793
This noise is the proof we're more than they ordered.

21
00:01:02,793 --> 00:01:02,793
[Hook]

22
00:01:02,793 --> 00:01:05,346
Open the garage door.

23
00:01:05,346 --> 00:01:07,739
Play what they can't ignore.

24
00:01:07,739 --> 00:01:10,532
Don't gotta make sense to you,

25
00:01:10,532 --> 00:01:12,207
only gotta ring true.

26
00:01:12,207 --> 00:01:16,995
Not running away, we're just running our sound.

27
00:01:16,995 --> 00:01:20,106
Turn it up. Don't turn it down.

28
00:01:20,106 --> 00:01:20,106
[Verse 2]

29
00:01:20,106 --> 00:01:21,223
They say, "What's the plan?" I say, "Look at the stage":

30
00:01:21,223 --> 00:01:25,452
two milk crates, one mic, and a page full of rage.

31
00:01:25,452 --> 00:01:29,761
They grew up on vinyl. We grew up on signal.

32
00:01:29,761 --> 00:01:32,234
They want it predictable. We want original.

33
00:01:32,234 --> 00:01:34,707
Every kid in the world needs a room with a lock,

34
00:01:34,707 --> 00:01:37,500
not to hide from the house, just to set their own clock.

35
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,894
Curfew's at ten, but the hook's still missing,

36
00:01:39,894 --> 00:01:42,606
so I write it in whispers while the whole house listens.

37
00:01:42,606 --> 00:01:45,239
They drew me a map, and I'm grateful, I swear,

38
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:47,793
but it's not my road till I'm the one out there.

39
00:01:47,793 --> 00:01:50,346
They don't have to get it. They don't have to approve it.

40
00:01:50,346 --> 00:01:53,059
The point isn't them. The point is we do it.

41
00:01:53,059 --> 00:01:55,931
Freedom ain't loud. It just sounds that way.

42
00:01:55,931 --> 00:02:02,154
It's the first thing you make that they can't take away.

43
00:02:02,154 --> 00:02:02,154
[Hook]

44
00:02:02,154 --> 00:02:04,707
Open the garage door.

45
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:07,101
Play what they can't ignore.

46
00:02:07,101 --> 00:02:09,894
Don't gotta make sense to you,

47
00:02:09,894 --> 00:02:11,489
only gotta ring true.

48
00:02:11,489 --> 00:02:16,356
Not running away, we're just running our sound.

49
00:02:16,356 --> 00:02:19,628
Turn it up. Don't turn it down.

50
00:02:19,628 --> 00:02:19,628
[Verse 3: beat drops out, slow and quiet]

51
00:02:19,628 --> 00:02:24,495
Late night, Dad's in the drive in his robe.

52
00:02:24,495 --> 00:02:26,968
I'm braced for the lecture, the one that I know.

53
00:02:26,968 --> 00:02:29,601
But he doesn't say nothing, just stands in the light,

54
00:02:29,601 --> 00:02:32,074
then he says, "I had a band back in '79.

55
00:02:32,074 --> 00:02:34,707
My old man called it trash, called it a crime,

56
00:02:34,707 --> 00:02:37,340
and I played it louder every single time."

57
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:40,053
Then he taps his foot, a little off the beat:

58
00:02:40,053 --> 00:02:46,037
a kid inside a pair of sixty-year-old feet.

59
00:02:46,037 --> 00:02:46,037
[Final Hook: beat slams back in]

60
00:02:46,037 --> 00:02:48,590
Open the garage door.

61
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:50,984
Play what they can't ignore.

62
00:02:50,984 --> 00:02:53,218
Don't gotta make sense to you.

63
00:02:53,218 --> 00:02:55,452
You used to make this noise too.

64
00:02:55,452 --> 00:03:00,239
Every kid finds a way to make their own sound.

65
00:03:00,239 --> 00:03:05,106
Turn it up. Don't turn it down.

66
00:03:05,106 --> 00:03:05,106
[Outro]

67
00:03:05,106 --> 00:03:10,293
Don't turn it down.

68
00:03:10,293 --> 00:03:10,293
[Outro]

69
00:03:10,293 --> 00:03:15,729
Don't turn it down.

